{"seq":22,"slug":"cyberpsychology","title":"网络心理学","stage":"DONE","category":"psychology","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/cyberpsychology","rating":{"composite":3.67,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":4,"strategic":3.67},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"网络心理学\">网络心理学</h1><p>人类的心智是在面对面的部落生活里演化出来的：我们读对方的表情、听语气的颤抖、在彼此的目光里调节分寸。可是过去二十年，越来越多的相处搬到了屏幕背后——文字框、点赞、推荐流、语音助手、乃至会主动嘘寒问暖的 AI 伴侣。当承载关系的介质换了，心智的运转也随之被悄悄改写。网络心理学就是研究「人在数字环境中如何感知、思考、表达与连接」的学科，它既不是把传统心理学照搬到网上，也不是单纯讨论技术，而是追问：介质的特性如何反过来塑造了人。</p>\n<p>这个 hub 用四条递进的主线把这门学科串起来。</p>\n<p>第一条主线是基础与理论。它回答最根本的问题：当面对面的社会线索被剥掉，人为什么会变得更大胆、更坦诚、也更刻薄？匿名和异步如何让人在网上呈现一个与线下不尽相同的自我？文字、表情包、已读不回这些贫线索的通道，又如何承载起丰富的社会互动？这一章奠定的去抑制、在线自我与中介互动三个概念，是后面所有章节反复借用的理论地基。</p>\n<p>第二条主线把镜头转向个体的心理健康。当使用从「用」滑向「停不下来」，临床上如何界定问题性使用与成瘾？社交媒体究竟有没有引爆青少年的抑郁与焦虑——这场至今未有定论的因果争论该怎么读？无处不在的通知与多任务，正在如何重塑我们的注意力与记忆？</p>\n<p>第三条主线放大到人与人之间的社会行为：屏幕上的亲密关系如何萌芽、维系与破裂；同样的去抑制如何催生网络欺凌与群体攻击；算法与同温层又如何把一群普通人推向极化的两端。</p>\n<p>第四条主线走到正在发生的前沿：会陪你聊天的 AI 伴侣带来慰藉还是新型依赖；游戏化、VR 与元宇宙用临场感重新定义「在场」；以及当心理健康干预搬进 App，疗效与伦理该如何权衡。</p>\n<p>四条主线并非彼此孤立。理论是工具，健康是落点，社会行为是放大器，前沿是新变量在重演旧问题。读完它们，你会带走一个统一的视角：技术从不中立，它的设计选择持续地在塑造我们如何成为人。各章引言会进一步交代每章的边界与在全局中的位置。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations-theory","title":"基础与理论","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/cyberpsychology/foundations-theory","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"intro-and-online-disinhibition","title":"网络心理学导论与在线去抑制效应","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/cyberpsychology/foundations-theory/intro-and-online-disinhibition"},{"seq":2,"slug":"online-self-and-identity","title":"在线自我与身份建构","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/cyberpsychology/foundations-theory/online-self-and-identity"},{"seq":3,"slug":"screen-mediated-interaction","title":"屏幕中介的社会互动","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/cyberpsychology/foundations-theory/screen-mediated-interaction"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"digital-use-wellbeing","title":"数字使用与心理健康","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/cyberpsychology/digital-use-wellbeing","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"problematic-use-and-addiction","title":"问题性互联网与手机使用","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/cyberpsychology/digital-use-wellbeing/problematic-use-and-addiction"},{"seq":2,"slug":"social-media-and-mental-health","title":"社交媒体与心理健康（青少年）","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/cyberpsychology/digital-use-wellbeing/social-media-and-mental-health"},{"seq":3,"slug":"attention-multitasking-cognition","title":"注意力、多任务与认知影响","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/cyberpsychology/digital-use-wellbeing/attention-multitasking-cognition"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"online-social-behavior","title":"在线社会行为","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/cyberpsychology/online-social-behavior","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"online-relationships-intimacy","title":"网络人际与亲密关系","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/cyberpsychology/online-social-behavior/online-relationships-intimacy"},{"seq":2,"slug":"cyberbullying-online-aggression","title":"网络欺凌与在线攻击","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/cyberpsychology/online-social-behavior/cyberbullying-online-aggression"},{"seq":3,"slug":"online-communities-polarization","title":"网络社群与群体极化","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/cyberpsychology/online-social-behavior/online-communities-polarization"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"frontiers-applications","title":"前沿与应用","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/cyberpsychology/frontiers-applications","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"hci-and-ai-companions","title":"人机交互与 AI 伴侣","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/cyberpsychology/frontiers-applications/hci-and-ai-companions"},{"seq":2,"slug":"gaming-vr-metaverse-psychology","title":"游戏化、VR 与元宇宙心理","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/cyberpsychology/frontiers-applications/gaming-vr-metaverse-psychology"},{"seq":3,"slug":"digital-mental-health-ethics","title":"数字心理健康干预与伦理","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/cyberpsychology/frontiers-applications/digital-mental-health-ethics"}]}]}